From 028609dab147f7c15e9da129878a01bbf3698449 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 01:02:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoInfoScanner] Use a movie's identifier in its folder
 name again

Since 4b7c092e13 a movie's identifier is read only from its filename.
With folder names used, an identifier in the folder name such as
"Film (2010) {tmdb=603}/movie.mkv" is ignored and the movie is searched
for by title. A refresh sees the identifier, hands the movie to the
scanner and then silently takes the first search result.

When the filename has no identifier, look in the name the movie is
looked up by, as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 23e0da6421fbccfc177bc7c0f16c9832986d495c)
